comments.content:
The restore is unconditional: any string sitting at a tracked path is overwritten with the original `$VAR` text. Since `saveSettings` is invoked from `LoadedSettings.setValue`, a user deliberately changing an env-backed setting to a literal (e.g. `config set model <literal>` while the file holds `"$MODEL"`, or the settings dialog changing `ui.theme`) will have that change silently reverted on write. `EnvVarMapping.resolvedValue` is recorded by `trackEnvVarMappings` but never read, so the intended guard is missing and the field is effectively dead. Restore only when the current value still equals the resolved value:
```ts
const envVarMap = new Map<string, EnvVarMapping>();
// ...
const mapping = envVarMap.get(pathStr);
if (mapping && typeof value === 'string' && value === mapping.resolvedValue) {
  (obj as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = mapping.originalValue;
}
```

comments.suggestion_code:
const envVarReference = envVarMap.get(pathStr);
if (envVarReference && typeof value === 'string') {
  (obj as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = envVarReference;

comments.existing_code:
const envVarReference = envVarMap.get(pathStr);
if (envVarReference && typeof value === 'string') {
  (obj as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = envVarReference;

